course: dictionary
lesson: 9117
title: Words that end in smith
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can be built from smaller parts, and those parts give you clues. Smith is a word on its own, and it is also the last part of words like blacksmith, goldsmith and locksmith.
explain: The first part of the word tells you what the smith works with. A blacksmith works with iron, a goldsmith works with gold, and a locksmith works with locks. «The village blacksmith made horseshoes and nails at a hot forge.» So a smith is a person who makes and shapes things out of metal.
explain: Smith can also be a family name, like the name of a real person. «Every Granny Smith tree comes from one seedling found in Australia around 1868 by Maria Ann Smith.» Here Smith is a name, not a job. Check by swapping in a job word: if the sentence stops making sense, the word is probably a name.
fact: A smith is a person who makes and shapes things out of metal.
fact: A blacksmith works with iron, and a goldsmith works with gold.
fact: Other words ending in -smith include silversmith, locksmith and wordsmith.
fact: Smith is one of the most common family names in English-speaking countries.
fact: Many family names come from old jobs, and Smith is the commonest of them.
exercise: «The village blacksmith made horseshoes at a hot forge.» What is a blacksmith? | *A person who makes things out of metal | A person who sells books | A person who grows apples | A person who writes stories
exercise: Which word means a smith who works with gold? | Wordsmith | *Goldsmith | Locksmith | Blacksmith
exercise: «Every Granny Smith tree comes from one seedling found in Australia around 1868 by Maria Ann Smith.» Is Smith a job or a name here? | A kind of forge | A job, like a blacksmith | *A family name | A metal
test: Which word means a smith who works with locks? | A silversmith | *A locksmith | A blacksmith | A goldsmith
test: Smith is a common word for what? | A tree | A kind of metal | *A family name in English-speaking countries | A town in Australia
exam: Which metal does a silversmith work with? | Gold | *Silver | Copper | Iron
